<title>BELGIUM: Spain's Aznar says EMU timetable must be met.</title>
<headline>Spain's Aznar says EMU timetable must be met.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Prime Minister Jose. Maria Aznar said on Tuesday that the treaty requirements for economic and monetary union (EMU) must be respected.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a treaty and there is a timetable to respect,&quot; Aznar told Spanish reporters on the margins of a meeting of EU centrist leaders in Brussels.</p>
</text>
